# =====================================================================
# Release V155 -- Day Book action counts: Open Plans / Recalls need an ACTIVE patient
# =====================================================================
# The four Day Book tiles applied three different patient rules between them:
#   Cancellations To Rebook / DNAs To Rebook : JOIN Dim_Patients ... AND Active = 1
#   Open Plans / Recalls To Action           : no patient filter at all
# So plans and recalls belonging to patients the practice had already marked inactive were still
# being counted and shown against the practitioner, which is part of why the counts read too high.
# Both now use the same Active = 1 join. No new columns; the aggregate is a DROP/CREATE full
# rebuild, so the corrected counts land on the next run.
#
# NOT addressed here (raised separately): the counts still have no recency horizon, and
# Rebooked_Status compares BOOKING time to the cancellation, so a patient who had already booked a
# later appointment before cancelling -- and then attended it -- stays on the list for ever.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V155__daybook_counts_active_patients_only.manifest
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Site_Practitioner_Current.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
